    "question": "A restaurant makes 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day. If the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs every day, how many pizzas and hot dogs will it make in June?",
    "gold": "4800",
    "answer": "If the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs and 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day, it makes 60+40 = <<60+40=100>>100 pizzas.\nThe total number of pizzas and hot dogs it makes in a day is 100+60 = <<100+60=160>>160\nIn June, with thirty days, the restaurant will make 30*160 = <<30*160=4800>>4800 pizzas and hot dogs in total.\n#### 4800"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of pizzas and hot dogs the restaurant will make in June, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of pizzas made each day:**\n   The restaurant makes 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day. Since the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs every day, the number of pizzas made each day is:\n   \\[\n   60 + 40 = 100\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of days in June:**\n   June has 30 days.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of pizzas made in June:**\n   Since the restaurant makes 100 pizzas each day, the total number of pizzas made in June is:\n   \\[\n   100 \\times 30 = 3000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of hot dogs made in June:**\n   Since the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs each day, the total number of hot dogs made in June is:\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 30 = 1800\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total number of pizzas and hot dogs made in June:**\n   The total number of pizzas and hot dogs made in June is the sum of the total number of pizzas and the total number of hot dogs:\n   \\[\n   3000 + 1800 = 4800\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of pizzas and hot dogs the restaurant will make in June is \\(\\boxed{4800}\\).",
